{title: The Lord Builds The House}
{subtitle: Psalms 127:1}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]A song of as[Bb]cents from Solo[F/A]mon
Unless the [Gm]Lord builds the [Eb]house
Its builders labor in [Bb]vain
Unless the Lord watch[F/A]es over the c[Eb]ity
The watchman keeps guard in vain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Lord builds the [Bb]house
The Lord [F]watches over the c[Gm]ity
Our labor is [Eb]vain without Him
He gives us the [Bb]victory [F][Gm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]In vain you rise [Bb]early
And stay up late to [F]toil
Eating the bread of anx[Gm]ious work
Trying to fulfill your [Eb]goal
But the Lord gives [Bb]sleep
To the one he [F]loves
Resting in His [Eb]sovereign grace
Away from the [Bb]waves
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Lord builds the house
The Lord [F]watches over the c[Gm]ity
Our labor is [Eb]vain without Him
He gives us the [Bb]victory [F][Gm][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Look, [Bb]children are a heritage
From the [F]Lord himself
The [Gm]fruit of the womb is a reward
A bles[Eb]sing in life
Like [Bb]arrows in the hand
Of [F]a warrior strong
So are the [Gm]sons of one's youth
[Eb]Where they belong
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The Lord builds the [Bb]house
The [F]Lord watches over the [Gm]city [Eb]
Amen
{end_of_verse}

